{
  "title": "GameSessionWatcher.getGameView() copies a live game off the game thread",
  "description": "GameSessionWatcher.getGameView() calls game.copy() on whatever \
thread the watcher attach RPC arrives on (its own comment admits 'can be called \
outside of the game thread'). Copying an object graph that the game thread is \
concurrently mutating can throw ConcurrentModificationException or produce a \
corrupt view. An exception here propagates out of GameController.watch -> \
gameWatchStart returns false -> the client silently drops the watch pane -> \
wait-for-watching 408 (same signature as the DUELING-registration race, but a \
separate hole). It is also slow (existing instrumentation logs elapsedMs; 168ms+ \
observed), which holds Session.callBackLock longer and increases the chance that \
concurrent GAME_UPDATE callbacks hit the 50ms tryLock timeout in \
Session.fireCallback and get silently dropped. Fix direction: build the initial \
watcher view via the game thread (or from the last authoritative cached view) \
instead of copying a live game from an RPC thread. Found during the \
wait-for-watching flake investigation; no direct CI failure attributed yet, so \
verify it can actually fire before large refactors.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "golden-tests",
    "server",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-01T18:40:00.000000-07:00",
